    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 032015\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n115 PM PDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Dry conditions and above normal temperatures will continue\n  through next week. \n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...through Friday.\n\nPersistent ridging over the Western US will allow for warmer than \nnormal temperatures to continue through next week. A weak shortwave \nwill approach the coast of Central California tomorrow, lifting into \nnorthern California and drifting through the Great Basin on late \nSunday through Monday. This shortwave will bring increased cloud \ncover and gentle southeasterly breezes to the region. It will also \nknock 500 mb heights down slightly, resulting in temperatures \nholding steady around 3 to 6 degrees above normal as we start next \nweek. 500 mb heights will rebound as the shortwave clears out and \nridging builds behind it during the middle of the week. These rising \n500 mb heights will allow for temperatures to increase, topping out \naround 5 to 10 degrees above normal during the middle of the week. \nThese hotter than normal temperatures will result in widespread \nMinor-to-Moderate HeatRisk (Levels 1 and 2 of 4, respectively) with \nMajor HeatRisk (Level 3 of 4) creeping into the lowest elevations of \nDeath Valley on Wednesday and Thursday. Hotter than normal \ntemperatures and dry conditions will continue through the end of the \nwork week as ridging persists over the area. \n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 18Z Forecast Package...Winds \nwill remain light and follow typical daily directional patterns \nthrough Sunday. The chance of seein* Dry conditions and above normal temperatures will continue through \n next week. g sustained speeds of 10 knots or greater remains \nless than 10 percent, although a random gust to 15 knots cannot be\nruled out during peak afternoon heating today and Sunday. VFR \nconditions will prevail through Sunday with only a few high clouds\nwith bases AOA 20kft AGL expected. \n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 18Z Forecast Package...Light winds following \ntypical daily directional patterns are expected at regional TAF \nsites through Sunday. Breezy conditions are expected each afternoon \nin the Owens Valley, but gusts should remain 20 knots or less today \nand less than 25 knots on Sunday. VFR conditions will prevail \nthrough Sunday with only a few high clouds with bases AOA 20kft AGL \nexpected. \n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Stessman\nAVIATION...Planz\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
